{"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"Sessions","modules":[{"name":"Sessions"}],"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"Sessions"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/sessions"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Put every event a tracker tracks in a session, and sample whole sessions."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sessions are opt-in. Add the sessions enricher to the ones a tracker is built with, and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tracker’s worker sets each record’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey","type":"reference"},{"text":" to its session’s identifier. A session goes on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"while each event comes less than the timeout (30 minutes by default) after the one before it,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measured between the records’ timestamps. The first event after a longer gap starts a new session.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The enricher tracks "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionStarted","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" before each session’s first event, and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"before that from the second session on, carrying the ended session’s duration. A run’s last session"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has no "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":": a session ends only when an event comes after the timeout. Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kinds:"},{"type":"text","text":" to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"track only one kind of session event, or neither; every record still carries its key."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A session’s identifier is a version 7 UUID: the session’s start in Unix milliseconds, then random"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bits. It is held in the enricher’s memory only, never written to disk, and a new tracker, as on the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"next launch, starts a new session. Records a store kept from an earlier run carry no key."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sampler.sessions(rate:)"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps or drops every record of a session alike, its session events with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it, by the record’s "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". It needs the sessions enricher among the tracker’s enrichers."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the app, device, operating system, locale and network an event was tracked on, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"StandardContext","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". For the app’s opens and moves to the background, use "},{"code":"LifecycleTracking","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its "},{"code":"ApplicationOpened","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" after a long time in the background starts a new session here, though"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neither module knows about the other."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Sessions","import Trackers","","let tracker = Tracker(enrichers: [try .sessions(timeout: .seconds(15 * 60), kinds: [.started])])","tracker.track(SignedUp(plan: \"pro\"))  \/\/ tracks SessionStarted, then SignedUp, both with the same SessionKey"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The guide "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/sessionsandstandardcontext"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers sessions beside the standard context, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/samplingevents"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"covers sampling."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Putting events in sessions","anchor":"Putting-events-in-sessions","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/Events\/Enricher\/sessions(kinds:file:fileID:function:line:column:)","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/Events\/Enricher\/sessions(timeout:kinds:file:fileID:function:line:column:)","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEventKind","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/NonPositiveSessionTimeout"]},{"title":"Reading a record’s session","anchor":"Reading-a-records-session","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionKey"]},{"title":"Session events","anchor":"Session-events","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionStarted","doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/SessionEnded"]},{"title":"Sampling whole sessions","anchor":"Sampling-whole-sessions","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Sessions\/documentation\/Sessions\/Trackers\/Sampler\/sessions(where:rate:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://Sessions/documentation/Sessions/SessionEnded/duration":{"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kin